---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Service",
  "name": "Marketing Automation Consulting",
  "serviceType": "Marketing Automation Consulting",
  "provider": { "@type": "Person", "name": "Pravine Manivannan", "url": "https://pravinemani.com/" },
  "areaServed": "Worldwide",
  "description": "Lead pipelines. Lifecycle email. CRM and webhook wiring. Stripe subscriptions. Code-first marketing infrastructure on Vercel, Resend, Supabase.",
  "url": "https://pravinemani.com/services/marketing-automation/"
};
---

<Base title="Marketing Automation Consulting · Lead Pipelines · Pravine Mani" description="Lead pipelines. Lifecycle email. CRM and webhook wiring. Stripe subscriptions. Code-first marketing infrastructure on Vercel, Resend, Supabase." jsonLd={jsonLd}>

<section class="page-hero">
  <div class="breadcrumb">
    <a href="/services/" style="color: var(--text-dim);">services</a>
    <span style="color: var(--text-muted, #444);">/</span>
    <span class="you">marketing automation</span>
  </div>
  <h1>Marketing automation.<br><span class="accent">In code. Without the SaaS tax.</span></h1>
  <p class="lead">Lead capture. CRM wiring. Lifecycle email. Subscription payments. Static + UGC creative generation. Built as code on Vercel, Resend, Supabase, Stripe + Higgsfield / GPT Image 2 / Nano Banana for media. No Zapier. No Make. No $300/mo platform fee. Owned outright. Debuggable when something breaks.</p>
  <div class="cta-row">
    <a href="/services/" class="cta-btn secondary">All engagement shapes</a>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="vert-grid">

    <article class="vert-card" id="pipelines">
      <div class="vert-head"><span class="vert-id">01</span><h2>Lead pipelines</h2></div>
      <p>Facebook Lead Ads or LinkedIn Lead Gen Forms → HMAC-verified webhook → Supabase or your CRM. Observable. Idempotent. Debuggable.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>FB Lead Ads / LinkedIn Lead Gen webhook → CRM</li>
        <li>HMAC signature verification on every event</li>
        <li>Idempotency keys to survive retries safely</li>
        <li>Admin portal surface so sales sees the leads</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="vert-card" id="email">
      <div class="vert-head"><span class="vert-id">02</span><h2>Lifecycle email</h2></div>
      <p>Onboarding sequences. Activation nudges. Dunning. Re-engagement. Resend or Postmark for transactional. Beehiiv or Kit for broadcast. Founder-style copy. Reply-bait subjects.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Day-2 / Day-7 / Day-14 sequences calibrated to product</li>
        <li>Reply-bait subject patterns (not the "Welcome to..." template)</li>
        <li>Suppression + bounce handling baked in</li>
        <li>Open + reply tracking surfaced in the admin portal</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="vert-card" id="crm">
      <div class="vert-head"><span class="vert-id">03</span><h2>CRM + webhooks</h2></div>
      <p>HubSpot. Attio. Pipedrive. Pick one. Wire it properly. Or skip CRM entirely and build a Supabase-backed admin portal that does only what you need. The right call depends on team size.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Two-way sync with your CRM</li>
        <li>Webhook fan-out (one event → many destinations)</li>
        <li>Slack notifications on high-signal events</li>
        <li>Decision matrix: when to skip the CRM entirely</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="vert-card" id="stripe">
      <div class="vert-head"><span class="vert-id">04</span><h2>Stripe + subscriptions</h2></div>
      <p>Stripe Checkout. Customer Portal. Webhooks. Idempotent event handlers. Dunning emails wired through your lifecycle stack. Annual plans, coupons, metered billing where they fit.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Stripe Checkout in 60 lines, not a Zapier graph</li>
        <li>Webhook handler with idempotency-key store</li>
        <li>Dunning + grace periods, cancellation flows</li>
        <li>Revenue dashboards in the admin portal</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="vert-card" id="creative">
      <div class="vert-head"><span class="vert-id">05</span><h2>Creative generation (static)</h2></div>
      <p>One brief → N image and copy variants for an ad set. Brand-tone guardrails baked in. GPT Image 2 + Higgsfield + Nano Banana under the hood. Approve, reject, regenerate. Built for agencies running paid creative at volume.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Brief schema: hook, product, audience, tone, output count</li>
        <li>Per-variant brand-tone guard: tested against a golden set</li>
        <li>Approval workflow with reject + regenerate loop</li>
        <li>Cost ceiling per brief (you set the cap, the system stops)</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="vert-card" id="ugc">
      <div class="vert-head"><span class="vert-id">06</span><h2>UGC video generation</h2></div>
      <p>UGC-style ad video at volume. Higgsfield Marketing Studio: avatar + product + hook + setting → 9:16 / 1:1 / 16:9 outputs. The pipeline that replaces a 6-person production crew for the test phase of an ad campaign.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Avatar pool: preset library + custom Soul Character training</li>
        <li>Product imports via URL or uploaded images</li>
        <li>Hook + setting selection per variant</li>
        <li>Output ladder: 4 variants → pick winner → scale to 20</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="section-head reveal">
    <div class="title-block">
      <div class="label">how it works</div>
      <h2>Engagement shapes for marketing automation.</h2>
      <p>Same three engagement shapes across all focus areas. Full ladder and pricing brackets at <a href="/services/">/services</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="vert-engagements">
    <a href="/services/#audit" class="vert-eng"><span class="lab">FUNNEL AUDIT</span><span class="when">FIXED-SCOPE WEEK · MID 4-FIG</span></a>
    <a href="/services/#sprint" class="vert-eng"><span class="lab">PIPELINE SPRINT</span><span class="when">FIXED-SCOPE BUILD · MID 4-FIG</span></a>
    <a href="/services/#custom" class="vert-eng"><span class="lab">FULL-STACK BUILD</span><span class="when">QUOTE-BASED · LOW 5-FIG+</span></a>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="vert-cta reveal" style="text-align: center;">
    <p style="margin: 0;">A pipeline to scope? <a href="/contact/" style="color: var(--green); border-bottom: 1px dashed var(--green);">Send the brief →</a></p>
  </div>
</section>

</Base>
